: ASM_ARCH=x86_64_nasm_gnu,x86_64_nasm_macho :
: BLOCK_TEST :
: RUN_ASM :

:/
Expected: storing 4294967296u64 through ptr u64 preserves all 64 bits.
The x86_64 GNU backend currently stores 0 by emitting MOV qword [ptr], 4294967296.
MOV qword [ptr], imm64 cannot be encoded, so the upper 32 bits are lost.
The local initializer is zero to isolate this store from initialization.
/:
@[inline(never)]
function write483(ptr u64 target) -> i0 {
    dref target = 4294967296u64;
}

start() {
    u64 value = 0;
    write483(ref value);
    if value != 4294967296u64; { exit 1; }
    exit 42;
}

:/ OUTPUT
@exit_code=42
/:
